& =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=v(u-1)^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=v{u}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2(u-1)v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =(u-1)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2uv & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & ={u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2(u-1)v & (u-1)^{2} \\\\ 2uv & {u}^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(u-1)v\\cdot {u}^{2}-(u-1)^{2}\\cdot 2uv \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}(u-1)v-2u(u-1)^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 2{u}^{2}(u-1)v-2u(u-1)^{2}v & =0 \\\\ 2u(u-1)v(u-(u-1)) & =0 \\\\ 2u(u-1)v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $2u(u-1)v=0$ defines the lines $u=0,$ $u=1,$ and $v=0$ in the $uv$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d7ca0aa0-a220-5bdc-b0d2-65b3a735f48d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{15}{7